{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.16","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":143678}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"4e830f6b","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# **Solar Filament Segmentation Challenge 2026**\n\n# Solar filament CV: train, evaluate, and export\n\n## Gregory Kojadinovich II\n\n\n**Kaggle GPU pipeline:** grayscale observations + COCO annotations -> day-grouped train/tuning/holdout -> pretrained U-Net -> threshold/area calibration -> individual masks -> full-resolution COCO RLE CSV. An intensity/contrast CV baseline is evaluated on the same splits. Run on Kaggle with the competition data attached, a GPU accelerator, and Internet enabled for installation and pretrained weights. Default: 20 epochs; this is a starting configuration, not a demonstrated optimal model.\n\n## Competition and paper requirements verified November 12, 2026\n- [Live overview](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/filament-segmentation-2026/overview): leaderboard **Panoptic Quality (PQ)**, not the anomaly papers' F1. Final judging is **70% quantitative, 30% qualitative**. F1 and PQ are objective given labels; annotator variation and the qualitative rubric introduce separate uncertainty/judgment.\n- CSV: `filament_id,segmentation_rle`, one row per filament. IDs preserve the image stem and add unique suffixes. Counts are compressed COCO RLE for **2048 x 2048** masks, not the example notebooks' 512 x 512 output. No invented empty-filament fallback.\n- Final evaluation needs a **four-page PDF**, [organizer template](https://www.overleaf.com/read/vjztpvrnbrdh#43fbbe), public Git repository, pinned packages, this notebook and saved weights for inference without retraining, plus the [final submission form](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfyrM4dhc8QzxR90PtF6fb018KPf0S0Cbf5hPqMuUognmzQsA/viewform?usp=dialog). The page states November 15, 2026, 11:59 pm CDT; confirm that stated timezone because November normally uses CST.\n- Old Dice wording remains on the page. Local class-agnostic PQ below is a transparent diagnostic, not a reproduction of all private server checks. Compare with the [organizer's self-evaluation notebook](https://www.kaggle.com/code/azimahmadzadeh/self-evaluation-notebook).\n\n## Research and model selection\nThe ESAIR 2026 poster describes **U-Net + MIoU -> geometry/spine grouping -> ConvNeXt chirality classification**. Supervised SVM and unsupervised one-class SVM in the 2025 papers classify **image quality**, not filament pixels. One-class SVM is not supervised binary SVM. Here, all chirality categories are merged into binary filament foreground; classification is not needed for the CSV.\n\n\nSources: [SoftwareX 2025](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.softx.2025.102120), [ICDMW 2025](https://doi.org/10.1109/ICDMW69685.2025.00235), supplied [ESAIR poster](./ESAIRPoster/GRF_Poster_04.2026.pdf), and [research summaries](./solar_filament_data_and_research.ipynb). Quality-control F1 scores are not segmentation results. Kaggle upload is off by default; the paper/form submission is separate.","metadata":{}},{"id":"d9a8b9a1","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Import libraries and configure the experiment\n\nThe setup cell installs only the segmentation dependencies, using the selected notebook kernel. Keep Kaggle's matched PyTorch/torchvision GPU installation. Exact installed versions are recorded after execution. For offline reproduction, install recorded dependencies and set `RUN_TRAINING=False`, `RUN_CALIBRATION=False` and `CHECKPOINT_INPUT_DIR` to the attached saved experiment folder; weights and selected parameters are loaded without downloading ImageNet weights.\n\nIf you change the architecture or split, use a new `RUN_NAME`. Never treat a short debugging run as publication evidence.","metadata":{}},{"id":"setup-dependencies","cell_type":"code","source":"%pip install -q 'segmentation-models-pytorch>=0.3.3,<0.7' pycocotools scipy\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-13T06:01:41.939841Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-13T06:01:41.940608Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-13T06:01:45.195241Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-13T06:01:41.940578Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-13T06:01:45.194518Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Note: you may need to restart the kernel to use updated packages.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"id":"config","cell_type":"code","source":"import csv\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.metadata\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport random\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom functools import lru_cache\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.ndimage as ndi\nfrom scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment\nfrom PIL import Image\nimport pycocotools.mask as mask_utils\nimport segmentation_models_pytorch as smp\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\nfrom tqdm.auto import tqdm\n\nCFG = dict(seed=2026, image_size=512, batch_size=8, epochs=20,\n           learning_rate=3e-4, encoder='resnet18', architecture='Unet',\n           pretrained=True, workers=0, tune_fraction=0.15, holdout_fraction=0.15,\n           tune_image_limit=32, thresholds=[0.35, 0.5, 0.65],\n           min_areas=[64, 256], contrast_thresholds=[0.025, 0.04, 0.06])\nRUN_NAME = 'unet_resnet18_gray_512_seed2026'\nRUN_TRAINING = True\nRUN_CALIBRATION = True\nSMOKE_TEST = False\nSUBMIT_TO_KAGGLE = True\nDATA_ROOT_OVERRIDE = None\nCHECKPOINT_INPUT_DIR = None  # Path to an attached experiment folder for inference-only reproduction.\nOUTPUT_DIR = (Path('/kaggle/working') if Path('/kaggle/working').is_dir()\n              else Path.cwd() / 'cv_outputs') / RUN_NAME\nOUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nINPUT_DIR = Path(CHECKPOINT_INPUT_DIR) if CHECKPOINT_INPUT_DIR else OUTPUT_DIR\nCHECKPOINT_PATH = INPUT_DIR / 'best_model.pt'\nCOMPETITION = 'filament-segmentation-2026'\nDATASET_NAME = 'MAGFiLO_1.0_Kaggle_2026'\nANNOTATION_NAME = 'MAGFiLO_1.0_Annotations_kaggle2026_train.json'\nFULL_SHAPE = (2048, 2048)\n\nrandom.seed(CFG['seed'])\nnp.random.seed(CFG['seed'])\ntorch.manual_seed(CFG['seed'])\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(CFG['seed'])\ntorch.backends.cudnn.benchmark = False\ntorch.backends.cudnn.deterministic = True\nDEVICE = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\nif DEVICE.type == 'cpu':\n    print('WARNING: CPU selected. Enable a Kaggle GPU before full training.')\nif CFG['image_size'] % 32 or CFG['batch_size'] < 2 or CFG['epochs'] < 1:\n    raise ValueError('Use image_size divisible by 32, batch_size >= 2, and epochs >= 1.')\nprint('Device:', DEVICE, 'outputs:', OUTPUT_DIR)\n\ndef write_json(path, value):\n    Path(path).write_text(json.dumps(value, indent=2, allow_nan=False))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-13T06:01:45.196889Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-13T06:01:45.197232Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-13T06:01:58.773509Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-13T06:01:45.197207Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-13T06:01:58.772745Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Device: cuda outputs: /kaggle/working/unet_resnet18_gray_512_seed2026\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"id":"b1218f1d","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Load training data and prevent annotation leakage\n\nMultiple annotator-specific image IDs refer to the same JPEG. Each annotation set remains a separate supervised target; splits are grouped by **observing day** so a physical image and same-day observations cannot leak across partitions. Training targets are unions of filaments **within one annotation set**, never a union across annotators.\n\nWe use about 70% of days for fitting, 15% for tuning/checkpoint selection, and 15% as an untouched holdout. Calibration can use up to 32 tuning images to bound runtime; holdout evaluation uses all holdout images. Holdout results must not be used to retune. Image resizing is an explicit first baseline limitation; thin structures may disappear. A tiled/full-resolution ablation is future work.","metadata":{}},{"id":"load-split","cell_type":"code","source":"candidates = ([Path(DATA_ROOT_OVERRIDE)] if DATA_ROOT_OVERRIDE else [\n    Path('/kaggle/input/competitions') / COMPETITION / DATASET_NAME,\n    Path('/kaggle/input') / COMPETITION / DATASET_NAME,\n    Path.cwd() / 'data' / DATASET_NAME, Path.cwd() / DATASET_NAME])\nif DATA_ROOT_OVERRIDE is None and Path('/kaggle/input').is_dir():\n    candidates += sorted(Path('/kaggle/input').glob(f'*/{DATASET_NAME}'))\n    candidates += sorted(Path('/kaggle/input').glob(f'*/*/{DATASET_NAME}'))\nvalid_roots = [p for p in candidates if (p / 'train' / ANNOTATION_NAME).is_file()\n               and (p / 'test' / 'test_images').is_dir()]\nif not valid_roots:\n    raise FileNotFoundError('Attach the competition data or set DATA_ROOT_OVERRIDE to its dataset root.')\nDATA_ROOT = valid_roots[0]\ntrain_paths = sorted((DATA_ROOT / 'train' / 'train_images').glob('*.jpeg'))\ntest_paths = sorted((DATA_ROOT / 'test' / 'test_images').glob('*.jpeg'))\nif not train_paths or not test_paths:\n    raise FileNotFoundError('Train and test must both contain JPEG files.')\nwith (DATA_ROOT / 'train' / ANNOTATION_NAME).open() as stream:\n    coco = json.load(stream)\nrecords = coco['images']\nif len({r['id'] for r in records}) != len(records):\n    raise ValueError('Duplicate COCO image IDs.')\nrecords_by_name = defaultdict(list)\nannotations_by_id = defaultdict(list)\nfor record in records:\n    if (record['height'], record['width']) != FULL_SHAPE:\n        raise ValueError(f'Unexpected dimensions for {record[\"id\"]}')\n    records_by_name[record['file_name']].append(record)\nfor ann in coco['annotations']:\n    if ann.get('iscrowd', 0) != 0:\n        raise ValueError('Local PQ assumes individual non-crowd filaments.')\n    annotations_by_id[ann['image_id']].append(ann)\nknown_ids = {r['id'] for r in records}\nif set(annotations_by_id) - known_ids:\n    raise ValueError('Orphan annotation image IDs.')\nif len({a['id'] for a in coco['annotations']}) != len(coco['annotations']):\n    raise ValueError('Duplicate filament annotation IDs.')\ntrain_lookup = {p.name: p for p in train_paths}\nif set(records_by_name) - set(train_lookup):\n    raise FileNotFoundError('Annotations reference missing training files.')\nif set(train_lookup) & {p.name for p in test_paths}:\n    raise ValueError('Train/test filenames overlap.')\ndays = sorted({name[:8] for name in records_by_name})\nif len(days) < 6:\n    raise ValueError('Not enough observing days for three nonempty grouped splits.')\nrandom.Random(CFG['seed']).shuffle(days)\nn_tune = max(1, round(len(days) * CFG['tune_fraction']))\nn_holdout = max(1, round(len(days) * CFG['holdout_fraction']))\nif n_tune + n_holdout >= len(days):\n    raise ValueError('Tuning and holdout fractions leave no training days.')\nday_sets = dict(tune=set(days[:n_tune]), holdout=set(days[n_tune:n_tune+n_holdout]),\n                train=set(days[n_tune+n_holdout:]))\nsplit_names = {split: sorted(n for n in records_by_name if n[:8] in selected)\n               for split, selected in day_sets.items()}\nsplit_records = {split: [r for name in names for r in records_by_name[name]]\n                 for split, names in split_names.items()}\nfor first, second in itertools.combinations(day_sets, 2):\n    assert not day_sets[first] & day_sets[second]\nannotation_sha256 = hashlib.sha256((DATA_ROOT / 'train' / ANNOTATION_NAME).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\nmanifest = dict(seed=CFG['seed'], grouping='observation-day', annotation_sha256=annotation_sha256,\n                policy='separate annotator targets; union within each target', splits=split_names)\nwrite_json(OUTPUT_DIR / 'split_manifest.json', manifest)\nprint('Data root:', DATA_ROOT)\nprint('JPEGs:', len(train_paths), 'train,', len(test_paths), 'test')\nprint('Annotation sets:', len(records), 'filaments:', len(coco['annotations']))\nprint('Categories:', Counter(a['category_id'] for a in coco['annotations']))\nprint('Splits:', {s: (len(split_names[s]), len(split_records[s])) for s in split_names})\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-13T06:01:58.774471Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-13T06:01:58.774932Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-13T06:01:59.867203Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-13T06:01:58.77491Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-13T06:01:59.866372Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Data root: /kaggle/input/competitions/filament-segmentation-2026/MAGFiLO_1.0_Kaggle_2026\nJPEGs: 707 train, 180 test\nAnnotation sets: 1154 filaments: 8199\nCategories: Counter({3: 3074, 2: 2590, 1: 2535})\nSplits: {'tune': (103, 161), 'holdout': (105, 166), 'train': (499, 827)}\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"id":"dataset-masks","cell_type":"code","source":"@lru_cache(maxsize=128)\ndef small_image(filename):\n    with Image.open(train_lookup[filename]) as image:\n        if image.mode != 'L' or image.size != (2048, 2048):\n            raise ValueError(f'{filename}: expected 2048 x 2048 grayscale JPEG.')\n        image = image.resize((CFG['image_size'], CFG['image_size']), Image.Resampling.BILINEAR)\n        return np.asarray(image, dtype=np.float32) / 255.0\n\ndef ann_rle(annotation):\n    segmentation = annotation['segmentation']\n    if isinstance(segmentation, list):\n        if not segmentation or any(len(p) < 6 or len(p) % 2 for p in segmentation):\n            raise ValueError(f'Invalid polygon: {annotation[\"id\"]}')\n        rle = mask_utils.merge(mask_utils.frPyObjects(segmentation, *FULL_SHAPE))\n    elif isinstance(segmentation, dict):\n        if list(segmentation['size']) != list(FULL_SHAPE):\n            raise ValueError('RLE dimensions do not match the image.')\n        if isinstance(segmentation['counts'], list):\n            rle = mask_utils.frPyObjects(segmentation, *FULL_SHAPE)\n        else:\n            counts = segmentation['counts']\n            rle = dict(size=list(FULL_SHAPE), counts=counts.encode('ascii') if isinstance(counts, str) else counts)\n    else:\n        raise TypeError(f'Unsupported segmentation: {annotation[\"id\"]}')\n    if mask_utils.area(rle) <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(f'Empty ground-truth filament: {annotation[\"id\"]}')\n    return rle\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=512)\ndef gt_rles(image_id):\n    return [ann_rle(a) for a in annotations_by_id[image_id]]\n\ndef union_mask(rles):\n    if not rles:\n        return np.zeros(FULL_SHAPE, dtype=np.uint8)\n    return mask_utils.decode(mask_utils.merge(rles))\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=128)\ndef small_target(image_id):\n    full_mask = union_mask(gt_rles(image_id))\n    resized = Image.fromarray(full_mask).resize((CFG['image_size'], CFG['image_size']), Image.Resampling.NEAREST)\n    return np.asarray(resized, dtype=np.float32)\n\nclass FilamentDataset(Dataset):\n    def __init__(self, entries, augment=False):\n        self.entries = entries\n        self.augment = augment\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.entries)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, index):\n        record = self.entries[index]\n        image = small_image(record['file_name'])\n        target = small_target(record['id'])\n        if self.augment:\n            turns = random.randrange(4)\n            image, target = np.rot90(image, turns), np.rot90(target, turns)\n            if random.random() < 0.5:\n                image, target = np.fliplr(image), np.fliplr(target)\n        x = torch.from_numpy(np.ascontiguousarray((image - 0.5) / 0.5))[None]\n        y = torch.from_numpy(np.ascontiguousarray(target))[None]\n        return x, y\n\nexample = split_records['train'][0]\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10, 5))\naxes[0].imshow(small_image(example['file_name']), cmap='gray', vmin=0, vmax=1)\naxes[1].imshow(small_image(example['file_name']), cmap='gray', vmin=0, vmax=1)\naxes[1].contour(small_target(example['id']), levels=[0.5], colors=['red'], linewidths=0.5)\naxes[0].set_title(example['file_name']); axes[1].set_title('One annotator target (red)')\nfor axis in axes: axis.axis('off')\nfig.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / 'training_annotation.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-13T06:01:59.868323Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-13T06:01:59.868669Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-13T06:02:00.593192Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-13T06:01:59.868638Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-13T06:02:00.592371Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x500 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":4},{"id":"031bb37a","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Train the supervised model, then tune only on calibration data\n\nU-Net/ResNet18 predicts one filament probability per pixel, with Dice+BCE loss and paired geometric augmentation. Inputs are normalized grayscale in [-1, 1]; SMP adapts pretrained encoder weights to one input channel. Change `architecture` to `FPN` for an established-library architecture ablation, using a new run name. Reduce batch size if GPU memory is insufficient.\n\nCheckpoint selection uses tuning-set loss; threshold and minimum original-resolution instance area are selected by local PQ. The independent holdout is evaluated afterward. We do **not** retrain on holdout data, so the saved weights exactly reproduce the reported predictions. Twenty epochs and 512-pixel inputs are baseline settings requiring convergence and resolution studies.","metadata":{}},{"id":"train-model","cell_type":"code","source":"def build_model(config, pretrained=False):\n    constructors = {'Unet': smp.Unet, 'FPN': smp.FPN}\n    if config['architecture'] not in constructors:\n        raise ValueError('Supported architectures: Unet, FPN.')\n    return constructors[config['architecture']](encoder_name=config['encoder'],\n        encoder_weights='imagenet' if pretrained else None, in_channels=1, classes=1, activation=None)\n\ndef segmentation_loss(logits, target):\n    probabilities = logits.sigmoid()\n    intersection = (probabilities * target).sum(dim=(1, 2, 3))\n    denominator = probabilities.sum(dim=(1, 2, 3)) + target.sum(dim=(1, 2, 3))\n    dice = 1 - ((2 * intersection + 1) / (denominator + 1)).mean()\n    return 0.5 * F.binary_cross_entropy_with_logits(logits, target) + 0.5 * dice\n\nif RUN_TRAINING:\n    if CHECKPOINT_INPUT_DIR is not None:\n        raise ValueError('Use a new output run to train; do not overwrite attached inference weights.')\n    if CHECKPOINT_PATH.exists():\n        raise FileExistsError('Existing checkpoint: set RUN_TRAINING=False or choose a new RUN_NAME.')\n    model = build_model(CFG, pretrained=CFG['pretrained']).to(DEVICE)\n    train_loader = DataLoader(FilamentDataset(split_records['train'], augment=True),\n        batch_size=CFG['batch_size'], shuffle=True, num_workers=CFG['workers'],\n        drop_last=len(split_records['train']) % CFG['batch_size'] == 1)\n    tune_loader = DataLoader(FilamentDataset(split_records['tune']),\n        batch_size=CFG['batch_size'], shuffle=False, num_workers=CFG['workers'])\n    if len(train_loader) == 0 or len(tune_loader) == 0:\n        raise ValueError('No batches: increase training sample count or lower batch size.')\n    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=CFG['learning_rate'])\n    best_loss, history = float('inf'), []\n    started = time.perf_counter()\n    for epoch in range(CFG['epochs']):\n        totals = {}\n        for phase, loader in [('train', train_loader), ('tune', tune_loader)]:\n            model.train(phase == 'train')\n            total, count = 0.0, 0\n            with torch.set_grad_enabled(phase == 'train'):\n                for images, targets in tqdm(loader, desc=f'Epoch {epoch+1} {phase}'):\n                    images, targets = images.to(DEVICE), targets.to(DEVICE)\n                    if phase == 'train': optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n                    loss = segmentation_loss(model(images), targets)\n                    if not torch.isfinite(loss):\n                        raise FloatingPointError(f'Nonfinite loss in {phase}.')\n                    if phase == 'train':\n                        loss.backward()\n                        optimizer.step()\n                    total += loss.item() * len(images); count += len(images)\n            totals[phase] = total / count\n        history.append(dict(epoch=epoch+1, train_loss=totals['train'], tune_loss=totals['tune']))\n        print(history[-1])\n        if totals['tune'] < best_loss:\n            best_loss = totals['tune']\n            torch.save(dict(state_dict={k: v.detach().cpu() for k, v in model.state_dict().items()},\n                            config=dict(CFG), epoch=epoch+1, tune_loss=best_loss,\n                            annotation_sha256=annotation_sha256, smoke_test=SMOKE_TEST), CHECKPOINT_PATH)\n    write_json(OUTPUT_DIR / 'training_history.json', history)\n    write_json(OUTPUT_DIR / 'training_runtime.json', dict(seconds=time.perf_counter()-started,\n        device=str(DEVICE), gpu=torch.cuda.get_device_name(0) if DEVICE.type == 'cuda' else None))\n\nif not CHECKPOINT_PATH.is_file():\n    raise FileNotFoundError('Train first or attach the saved best_model.pt experiment.')\ncheckpoint = torch.load(CHECKPOINT_PATH, map_location='cpu', weights_only=True)\nif checkpoint['annotation_sha256'] != annotation_sha256:\n    raise ValueError('Checkpoint was trained against a different annotation file.')\nif checkpoint['smoke_test'] != SMOKE_TEST:\n    raise ValueError('Smoke-test checkpoint cannot be used for a competition run.')\nif checkpoint['config'] != CFG:\n    raise ValueError('Configuration differs from checkpoint; restore its config for reproduction.')\nmodel = build_model(checkpoint['config'], pretrained=False).to(DEVICE)\nmodel.load_state_dict(checkpoint['state_dict'], strict=True)\nmodel.eval()\nCHECKPOINT_SHA256 = hashlib.sha256(CHECKPOINT_PATH.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\nprint('Loaded best epoch:', checkpoint['epoch'], 'tuning loss:', checkpoint['tune_loss'])\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-13T06:02:00.595281Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-13T06:02:00.595604Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","text":"Warning: You are sending unauthenticated requests to the HF Hub. Please set a HF_TOKEN to enable higher rate limits and faster downloads.\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"config.json:   0%|          | 0.00/156 [00:00<?, ?B/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"e11915622f014ba3b400dff2e4904682"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"model.safetensors: reconstructing file:   0%|          |  0.00B / 46.8MB            ","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"34adffcfe37146b1a4565f7ce4a89d9a"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"model.safetensors: downloading bytes:           |  0.00B            ","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"95344afb46b94d93afbd2321e21bfeb1"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Epoch 1 train:   0%|          | 0/104 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id